          "title": "British Blockade",
          "subtitle": "Patience",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "British Blockade, also known as Parallels, is an English two-pack patience game in the blockade family."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "An old English patience whose name distinguishes it from French Blockade; Parallels refers to its row layout."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "1 players use the table arrangement described for British Blockade."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Two standard 52-card decks"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Two standard 52-card decks, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Lay out rows of tableau cards from two packs, then use the stock or reserve according to the patience layout."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
